# Line endings are pinned here because this project is edited on Windows and run on Linux.
#
# Without this file, `git add` on Windows warns that LF "will be replaced by CRLF" and a checkout on
# another machine would rewrite every file. For the shell scripts that is not cosmetic: a script with
# CRLF line endings fails on the server with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, and the failure appears
# when it is run, not when it is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
# Pictures and the database are binary; nothing may touch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.sqlite3 binary
